{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokesEigenvalues","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokesEigenvalues","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.quantum_dim_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.quantum_dim_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeStokesEigenvalues.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**`[2]_q` is bar-even:** `[2]_{q⁻¹} = [2]_q`, i.e. `q⁻¹ + (q⁻¹)⁻¹ = q + q⁻¹`.\n(The eigenvalue gap is invariant under the Hecke bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`; the linear\ncoefficient `q − q⁻¹` is not.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.quantum_dim_is_eigenvalue_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.quantum_dim_is_eigenvalue_gap","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeStokesEigenvalues.lean#L60-L65","doc":"**The quantum dimension `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` is the eigenvalue gap `λ₊ − λ₋`.**\n`q − (−q⁻¹) = q + q⁻¹`. This bar-even combination — not the bar-odd sum above — is what `τ`\nis built from (`TauQuantumIntegerForm`), which is why `τ` is bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_eigenvalues_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_eigenvalues_sum","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeStokesEigenvalues.lean#L55-L58","doc":"Their **sum is the linear coefficient `q − q⁻¹` of the monodromy quadratic** (`λ₊ + λ₋`), which is **bar-odd**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_eigenvalues_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_eigenvalues_prod","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeStokesEigenvalues.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The two Hecke eigenvalues have **product `−1`** (`λ₊ · λ₋`, the Hecke-generator determinant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_curvature_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.stokes_curvature_factors","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeStokesEigenvalues.lean#L42-L48","doc":"**The monodromy quadratic factors into the two Hecke eigenvalues.**\nThe characteristic polynomial `X² − (q − q⁻¹)X − 1` of the exchange monodromy factors as `(X − q)(X + q⁻¹)`:\nroots `λ₊ = q` (symmetric channel `L₊`) and `λ₋ = −q⁻¹` (antisymmetric channel `L₋`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}